<title>NETHERLANDS: Endemol shares jump on Sport 7 sale.</title>
<headline>Endemol shares jump on Sport 7 sale.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-11-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in television production and entertainment group Endemol jumped 3.30 guilders to 59.80 on Tuesday after the company announced it was transferring its stake in loss-making TV channel Sport 7 to its management.</p>
<p>&quot;The risks for Endemol have been eliminated, and that has been very positively interpreted by investors,&quot; said one dealer, adding &quot;short term it is a good move, but it means that if Sport 7 comes good, Endemol's revenues will be limited to programme-making.&quot;</p>
<p>The company said Endemol founders Joop Van Ende and John de Mol would acquire the stake at the initial price paid.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
